==English==
===Etymology===
[[appraise#Verb|to appraise]] + [[-al]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[judgment]] or [[assessment]] of the [[value]] of something, especially a [[formal]] one for loan or [[tax]]ation purposes.
# A [[judgment]] or [[assessment]] of the professional performance of someone, especially a [[subordinate]] .


== English ==
An appraisal, though done by a knowledgable person, does not necessarily correlate to that which someone is willing to pay for the item.  Ultimately market forces play a role in determining what an item is worth at any given time. 
